Project Focus: Real-Time Feature Store (02-realtime-feature-store)
This pipeline solves training-serving skew by storing features in an offline store (for historical model training) and materializing them to an online store (for sub-millisecond real-time scoring).

Step 1: Feature Definition (feature_store/features.py)
Create your entity and feature views using Feast's configuration framework:

Python
from datetime import timedelta
from feast import Entity, Field, FeatureView, FileSource, ValueType
from feast.types import Float32, Int64

# Define an entity for your data items (e.g., location, device, or user ID)
location_entity = Entity(
    name="location_id",
    value_type=ValueType.INT64,
    description="Unique identifier for the monitored location or field",
)

# Define offline data source (e.g., historical soil or weather measurements)
soil_offline_source = FileSource(
    name="soil_stats_source",
    path="data/soil_features.parquet",
    timestamp_field="event_timestamp",
    created_timestamp_column="created_timestamp",
)

# Define the Feature View
soil_feature_view = FeatureView(
    name="soil_feature_view",
    entities=[location_entity],
    ttl=timedelta(days=365),
    schema=[
        Field(name="N", dtype=Float32),
        Field(name="P", dtype=Float32),
        Field(name="K", dtype=Float32),
        Field(name="ph", dtype=Float32),
    ],
    online=True,
    source=soil_offline_source,
)
